# Select

A select is a compact choice control for a longer, familiar list.

These are civica.uk reference implementations for component authors. They do not replace native Home Assistant behaviour or demonstrate a connection to a live home.

## When to use it

Use it only after considering whether a shorter question or visible radio group would be clearer. The ten named civica palettes are an explicit settings use: the labels are familiar, the choice is reversible and keyboard selection is native.

## When not to use it

Do not use a multi-select list for rooms or hide two simple choices in a dropdown. Do not use the first option as an accidental answer to an unanswered question.

## Home Assistant adaptation

Preselect the saved palette when editing theme settings. Keep its name in text and provide an immediate visual preview; a colour swatch alone does not identify the choice. Selecting an appearance must not issue device commands or reset the selected Energy period.

## Accessibility and behaviour

Provide a visible label and useful hint. Keep the native select keyboard behaviour and avoid replacing it with a custom menu unless its full accessibility contract is implemented. Label a required unanswered option explicitly.

